ntastic he did a really good job  coaching that team  that's what i told him you know i just  thought i was like i thought you did a  really good job coaching your team  because  people talk about the end and kind of  their players who they joined up with  but there was a stretch there in the  middle where i don't think anyone was  predicting that the rams were going to  make it to victory lane and that's the  sign of an organization that um  that's that's built to last to be able  to respond to a tough stretch and that's  what they did  who do you get mistaken for  man damn that that  i don't know if i was ready for that one  um  [Music]  i don't know that  well you're in la i mean did you ever  been mistaken identity for an actor  uh i don't know i've gotten some johnny  knoxville comps  [Laughter]  uh you know there was like a a time  there um you know i kind of you know and  i'm the same age as matt weiner uh you  know former quarterback uh  you know but um those are two names that  have been thrown out there in the past i  don't know how accurate they are um and  then you know throughout the year i was  getting pepper with these questions  about this ted lasso guy so um i haven't  watched that show yet but i'm told that  i need to so amy and i may join up with  that show here soon i kind of see peter  brady from the brady bunch  you know what dan now that you mentioned  that i've heard about that and again  that was kind of before my time  uh which probably dates me a little bit  on the youthful side but i didn't join  up with that show as a young kid so well  if you google peter brady you might go  okay i okay he's got a point it's not  it's not an insult it's not an insult uh  that was a successful show yes it was  yes it was uh and johnny knoxville i  could see that you even have the the  voice kind of raspy in there i could see  that get those glasses on i could see  that  maybe bring johnny knoxville to practice  johnny had a great run man he's still  doin